Fixed in `77d25ec`. The `${VAR}` check now runs inside `nativeOverlay` and only over the values native rendering consumes, mirroring `personality.py`:
- the selection (`display.personality`);
- for the selected personality, `system_prompt`, `tone` and `style` of a structured definition, or the string/list itself;
- `agent.system_prompt` when nothing is selected;
- a personality name key containing `${`, since interpolating it could change which definition is selected.

`description`, which only `describe_personality` uses for list previews, and unselected definitions are ignored. Your `description: "${AO_REVIEW_LABEL}"` cases under both `personalities` and `agent.personalities` now launch. Interpolated selected `system_prompt` / `tone` / `style` / list entries and an interpolated selection are still refused. All are in `TestHooksIgnoreEnvExamplesInConfigComments`.

Fixed in `77d25ec`. The inherited-key filter now applies every dotenv layer native loads with override, in `load_hermes_dotenv` order (`overridingAssignments`):
1. `<HERMES_HOME>/.env` if it exists;
2. otherwise the project `.env` of every source checkout (the same `sourceRoots` the hook guards);
3. then any managed scope's `.env`.

A key assigned in any of them, even to empty, is no longer taken from AO's environment. If a layer cannot be read the way Hermes reads it, no inherited key is trusted. Your absent-home case now reports unknown, and your positive control still finds the key: with a harmless home `.env`, the project file loads without override. Regression: `TestInheritedCredentialClearedByProjectDotenv`.

Fixed in `77d25ec`. Python `str.strip()` semantics (`pyStrip`, built on `pyIsSpace`) now replace `strings.TrimSpace` everywhere AO mirrors a native strip, not just here:
- `HERMES_MANAGED_DIR`, `HERMES_HOME` and `LOCALAPPDATA`;
- `active_profile`;
- personality names and prompt text.

`\x1c/absolute/managed`, the U+001F variant and an NBSP prefix are all refused; they are cases in `TestHooksForceEnglishChromeAndRefuseDotenvOverrides`.

Fixed in `77d25ec`. The fallback no longer trusts the banner's clean marker. `SourceReleaseTag` now asks git directly in the launcher's checkout, with `--no-optional-locks` and a 10 s timeout:
- `rev-parse --verify HEAD^{commit}` must match the banner SHA;
- `status --porcelain --untracked-files=no` must be empty;
- the qualifying tag comes from `tag --points-at HEAD`.

A tracked modification such as your `locales/en.yaml` busy-text edit is refused even when a stored native stamp still says `dirty:false`. Without git, or if any git call fails, the fallback refuses. Regression: the tracked-modification case in `TestTaglessSourceBannerNeedsQualifiedTagAtHead`, built on real git.

